# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOCAL DEV database template — SyncBiz universal-music tooling
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Copy this file to  .env.development   (same folder).
#   2. Replace REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_LOCAL_PASSWORD with the password you
#      chose for the local "postgres" user during install.
#   3. Run:  npm run db:check   (verifies it's a safe LOCAL target).
#
# RULES:
#   • LOCAL Postgres only. Host MUST be localhost. Database MUST be syncbiz_dev.
#   • NEVER put production values here. NEVER share this file's real copy.
#   • .env.development is git-ignored; only THIS *.example is tracked.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Local PostgreSQL connection (localhost, database "syncbiz_dev").
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_LOCAL_PASSWORD@localhost:5432/syncbiz_dev

# Marks this as a non-production environment. The safety guard REQUIRES this to be
# "development" or "staging" before any migrate / backfill / rollback can run.
SYNCBIZ_ENV=development

# (Staging only — NOT needed for local dev.) The production DB host, so the guard can
# hard-block it. Leave commented out for local development.
# SYNCBIZ_PROD_DATABASE_HOST=
